WEBVTT

00:00:09.748 --> 00:00:11.708
AMOS:
Come on up. Take your seats.

00:00:11.875 --> 00:00:14.419
I told you these seats
would be worth waiting for.

00:00:14.586 --> 00:00:16.421
Come on!

00:00:18.757 --> 00:00:20.592
FRED:
It's the Irish! There's Troy!

00:00:20.884 --> 00:00:22.594
GEORGE: And Mullet!
FRED: And Moran!

00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:31.394
CROWD [CHANTING]:
Ireland! Ireland! Ireland!

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.610
GEORGE: Here come the Bulgarians!
FRED: Yes!

00:00:38.902 --> 00:00:40.278
ALL:
Whoa!

00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:46.243
GINNY:
Who's that?

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:49.913
That, sis, is the best Seeker
in the world.

00:00:51.998 --> 00:00:55.460
CROWD [CHANTING]:
Krum! Krum! Krum!

00:01:00.257 --> 00:01:01.466
HARRY, RON, FRED AND GEORGE:
Krum!

00:01:01.633 --> 00:01:04.135
-Yes!
-Whoo!

00:01:11.142 --> 00:01:13.019
Good evening!

00:01:13.478 --> 00:01:16.481
As Minister for Magic...

00:01:16.815 --> 00:01:19.818
...it gives me great pleasure...

00:01:20.485 --> 00:01:24.322
...to welcome
each and every one of you...

00:01:24.489 --> 00:01:30.328
...to the final
of the 422nd Quidditch World Cup!

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.330
Let the match...

00:01:32.539 --> 00:01:34.332
...begin!

00:01:40.463 --> 00:01:42.507
RON AND HARRY CHANTING:
Krum! Krum! Krum!

00:01:44.676 --> 00:01:48.305
[FRED AND GEORGE
SINGING GIBBERISH]

00:01:50.473 --> 00:01:52.058
There's no one like Krum.

00:01:52.309 --> 00:01:53.810
FRED: Krum?
-Dumb Krum?

00:01:53.977 --> 00:01:57.063
He's like a bird,
the way he rides the wind.

00:01:57.314 --> 00:02:00.191
-He's more than an athlete.
-Dumb Krum.

00:02:00.358 --> 00:02:01.568
He's an artist.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.987
-I think you're in love, Ron.
RON: Shut up.

00:02:04.321 --> 00:02:05.572
[SINGING]
Viktor, I love you

00:02:05.864 --> 00:02:07.490
Viktor, I do

00:02:07.532 --> 00:02:10.076
When we're apart
My heart beats only for you

00:02:11.536 --> 00:02:13.580
Sounds like the Irish
have got their pride on.

00:02:13.872 --> 00:02:15.540
ARTHUR:
Stop! Stop it!

00:02:16.207 --> 00:02:17.709
It's not the Irish.

00:02:18.877 --> 00:02:21.004
We've gotta get out of here. Now!

00:02:23.214 --> 00:02:25.550
MAN:
Get out, it's the Death Eaters!

00:02:25.592 --> 00:02:29.012
Get back to the Portkey, everybody,
and stick together!

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.890
Fred, George!
Ginny is your responsibility.

00:02:32.515 --> 00:02:34.225
Go!

00:02:34.517 --> 00:02:36.227
Harry!

00:02:40.023 --> 00:02:41.941
[DEATH EATERS
CHANTING INDISTINCTLY]

00:02:51.034 --> 00:02:53.244
GEORGE: Keep up, you lot!
-Harry!

00:02:54.537 --> 00:02:56.581
Harry! Harry!

00:03:44.295 --> 00:03:45.630
Morsmordre!

00:04:12.615 --> 00:04:13.992
RON:
Harry!

00:04:15.618 --> 00:04:18.663
-Where are you?
HERMIONE: Harry!

00:04:19.831 --> 00:04:22.667
RON:
We've been looking for you for ages!

00:04:23.668 --> 00:04:25.628
Thought we lost you, mate.

00:04:26.337 --> 00:04:28.339
HARRY:
What is that?

00:04:31.509 --> 00:04:33.553
WIZARDS:
Stupefy!

00:04:33.678 --> 00:04:34.971
ARTHUR:
Stop!

00:04:35.138 --> 00:04:37.474
That's my son!

00:04:38.516 --> 00:04:41.060
-Ron, Harry, Hermione, you all right?
-We came back for Harry.

00:04:41.227 --> 00:04:42.562
Which of you conjured it?

00:04:42.687 --> 00:04:44.856
-Crouch, you can't possi--
-Do not lie!

00:04:45.064 --> 00:04:47.066
You've been discovered
at the scene of the crime.

00:04:47.233 --> 00:04:49.235
-Crime?
-Barty! They're just kids.

00:04:49.527 --> 00:04:50.862
What crime?

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:53.573
It's the Dark Mark, Harry.
It's his mark.

00:04:53.698 --> 00:04:54.866
What, Voldemort?

00:04:56.075 --> 00:04:59.871
Those people tonight, in the masks,
they're his too, aren't they?

00:05:00.163 --> 00:05:02.373
-His followers?
-Yeah.

00:05:02.665 --> 00:05:04.542
Death Eaters.

00:05:05.168 --> 00:05:09.172
-Follow me.
-There was a man, before.

00:05:09.714 --> 00:05:11.007
There!

00:05:11.174 --> 00:05:13.676
All of you, this way!

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:15.720
ARTHUR:
A man, Harry?

00:05:15.887 --> 00:05:17.555
Who?

00:05:17.764 --> 00:05:19.724
I don't know.

00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:23.561
I didn't see his face.

00:05:39.744 --> 00:05:41.746
WOMAN:
Anything from the trolley?

00:05:43.748 --> 00:05:46.918
Anything from the trolley?

00:05:50.797 --> 00:05:52.632
Anything from the trolley, dears?

00:05:52.757 --> 00:05:54.926
RON:
Packet of Drooble's...

00:05:55.218 --> 00:05:56.928
...and a Licorice Wand.

00:05:58.555 --> 00:06:00.598
On second thought, just the Drooble's.

00:06:00.765 --> 00:06:04.769
-It's all right, I'll get it. Don't worry.
-Just the Drooble's. Thanks.

00:06:05.937 --> 00:06:08.439
Two Pumpkin Pasties, please.

00:06:13.778 --> 00:06:15.446
Thank you.

00:06:15.947 --> 00:06:18.241
WOMAN:
Anything sweet for you, dear?

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:21.452
Oh, no, I'm not hungry. Thank you.

00:06:22.328 --> 00:06:24.330
WOMAN:
Anything from the trolley?

00:06:24.581 --> 00:06:26.624
HERMIONE:
This is horrible.

00:06:26.791 --> 00:06:29.669
How can the Ministry
not know who conjured it?

00:06:29.794 --> 00:06:31.629
Wasn't there any security or...?

00:06:31.796 --> 00:06:34.632
Loads, according to Dad.

00:06:34.799 --> 00:06:38.761
That's what worried them so much.
Happened right under their noses.

00:06:41.264 --> 00:06:44.684
It's hurting again, isn't it?
Your scar.

00:06:44.809 --> 00:06:46.644
I'm fine.

00:06:48.646 --> 00:06:51.482
You know Sirius will
want to hear about this...

00:06:51.774 --> 00:06:55.778
...what you saw at the World Cup
and the dream.

00:07:03.995 --> 00:07:07.290
Hedwig. There we go.

00:07:46.412 --> 00:07:48.831
Clear the runway!

00:07:51.709 --> 00:07:53.878
-Aah!
ALL: Whoa!

00:07:54.045 --> 00:07:56.881
Well, there's something
you don't see every day.

